---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const githubActionsSnippet = `name: Repository standards
on: [push, pull_request]
permissions:
  contents: read
jobs:
  considered:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1
        with:
          persist-credentials: false
      - name: Install Considered
        env:
          CONSIDERED_VERSION: v0.1.10
          CONSIDERED_SHA256: 75d94d4929f493dbaa4fba1904728ed41022e141b417b13931da17eca6b4c2ba
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          tool_dir="$(mktemp -d)"
          archive="considered_\${CONSIDERED_VERSION}_linux_amd64.tar.gz"
          release="https://github.com/quitepicky/considered/releases/download/\${CONSIDERED_VERSION}"
          curl --fail --location --silent --show-error "$release/$archive" -o "$tool_dir/$archive"
          printf '%s  %s\\n' "$CONSIDERED_SHA256" "$tool_dir/$archive" | sha256sum --check -
          tar -xzf "$tool_dir/$archive" -C "$tool_dir"
          # Both binaries are inside the archive's versioned directory.
          echo "$tool_dir/considered_\${CONSIDERED_VERSION}_linux_amd64" >> "$GITHUB_PATH"
      - name: Check repository standards
        run: considered check`;

const outputCommands = `considered check --json
considered check --sarif`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="CI"
  description="Use Considered in CI and code scanning workflows."
  current="/ci/"
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1>CI</h1>
    <p>
      <code>considered check</code> exits non-zero for violations, invalid
      configuration, provider failures, and other execution errors. Variances
      and warnings stay visible without failing the check.
    </p>

    <h2>Exit codes</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Code</th>
          <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>0</code></td>
          <td>All checks pass.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>1</code></td>
          <td>One or more violations.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>2</code></td>
          <td>Usage, configuration, provider, or output error.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
      These codes describe <code>considered check</code>. Commands that write
      configuration, such as <code>init</code> and <code>variance add</code>,
      return <code>1</code> when the requested write or variance cannot be completed.
    </p>

    <h2>Machine-readable output</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={outputCommands} />

    <p>
      In SARIF, violations are emitted as errors, warnings as warnings, and
      variances as informational notes. Choose either <code>--json</code> or
      <code>--sarif</code>; using both is an error. Redirect stdout to a file when
      saving a report. Diagnostics are written to stderr.
    </p>

    <h2>GitHub Actions</h2>
    <p>
      Commit your <code>.considered.yaml</code>, then save this workflow as
      <code>.github/workflows/considered.yml</code> in the repository you want to
      check. It installs the published Linux x64 release, verifies its checksum,
      and adds both binaries to <code>PATH</code>. No Go build is required.
      Update the version and checksum together when upgrading.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock lang="yaml" code={githubActionsSnippet} />

    <h2>Considered's Windows release checks</h2>
    <p>
      Considered's own release workflow requires native x64 and ARM64 Windows
      jobs to validate and install its WinGet package before publishing. The
      jobs check both command aliases, the installed version, the bundled
      provider, package registration, and uninstall. The unpublished ZIPs are
      served over loopback for installation with their original checksums;
      this does not replace Microsoft's public-URL validation or malware scans.
      The publishing rebuild must match the tested Windows artifacts before the
      GitHub release becomes public. See the
      <a href="https://github.com/quitepicky/considered/blob/main/RELEASING.md">release guide</a>
      for test evidence and the distinction between submission and acceptance.
    </p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
